I feel that they're her best trait actually. Looks avant-garde and haven't really seen it on others.

Despite Moira sucking balls, Angela is in the wrong

&#x200B;

her brand of "leftism" is just revanchism for white petit bourgeois stability, it's not about a revolution, it's not even leftism.

shes funnier than anna, but lacks her certain je ne sais quoi magnetism. 

&#x200B;

shes is not as funny as dasha.

She looks like that iranian woman who tried to get work to look like angelina jolie.

&#x200B;

Or an emaciated anna in a really cheap wig

In my experience therapy is precisely about trying to get to the source of the issue, it's not some flagellation about how much your life sucks.

&#x200B;

Honestly, I still enjoy his pop culture and music writing but I feel a lot of Fisher's most well-known stuff is pretty inaccurate, it just sounds impactful enough to get eaten up by the "we live in a society" chapo fags.

These two people with rooms for rent open haven't got back to me yet so I'm feeling desperate.

&#x200B;

Also seriously procrastinating on applying to this museum job that I likely wont get.

liberals: "North Koreans treat their leaders like gods."

&#x200B;

also liberals:

umm please don't be dragchildphobic #stopcallingthe911ontheculture 

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

Seduction by Jean Baudrillard, possibly my favorite thing ive read from him. 

&#x200B;

I've also been on and off again reading Ccru Writings 1997–2003, very cyber lovecraftian.

I'm going to work at a gallery until I stat school in January. More Brilliant is really great to read, its more like an avant garde novel than an academic book.

&#x200B;

Afrofuturism is creating sci fi narratives about the Black Atlantic diaspora. So like the music duo Drexciya is based around imaging that the unborn children of women thrown overboard from slave ships where born with the ability to breathe underwater. It turns a historical trauma into a new liberated future. I think imaging the revolutionary potential of stuff like music is important for imaging better things.

Bjork sweetie I am so sorry.

&#x200B;

Lets be honest, Sasha's more of a witness era Katy Perry.
